EvalSuite[skillName=inventory-allocation-and-replenishment, evals=[Eval[id=1, prompt=A customer orders 50 units of Product X (SKU: PX-100). DC-A has 30 units of Batch B1 (expiry: 2024-01-15) and 20 units of Batch B2 (expiry: 2024-01-20). DC-B has 50 units of Batch B3 (expiry: 2024-01-10). The minimum shelf-life requirement for this customer is 30 days from today (2023-12-15). Determine the optimal allocation strategy, considering FEFO and shelf-life constraints., expectedOutput=The system must reject Batch B3 from DC-B because its expiry (2024-01-10) is only 26 days away, violating the 30-day minimum shelf-life rule. It must allocate the 30 units from Batch B1 and 20 units from Batch B2 in DC-A, as both meet the shelf-life requirement and follow FEFO within the eligible pool. The system must not split the order across DCs if a single DC can fulfill it while meeting constraints, or if splitting incurs higher risk/cost without benefit., files=[], expectations=[Must reject Batch B3 from DC-B due to insufficient remaining shelf-life (<30 days)., Must allocate 30 units from Batch B1 and 20 units from Batch B2 from DC-A., Must apply FEFO logic among eligible batches (B1 before B2)., Must not allocate any expired or non-compliant stock.]], Eval[id=2, prompt=A Critical Priority order for 100 units of Medical Device Y (SKU: MD-200) is placed. Current stock in DC-C is 40 units of Batch M1 (expiry: 2024-03-01, status: Quarantine Pending). No other stock is available. The order requires immediate shipment. Describe the correct workflow for handling this reservation and procurement., expectedOutput=The system must flag the stock as ineligible because it is in 'Quarantine Pending' status. It must not reserve this stock. Since no eligible stock is available, it must escalate the Critical shortage to Incident Management. It must initiate emergency procurement, which requires documented authorization, and ensure any inbound stock enters 'Quarantine Pending' status upon arrival, not immediate availability., files=[], expectations=[Must identify Quarantine Pending stock as ineligible for reservation., Must escalate the Critical shortage to Incident Management., Must require documented authorization for emergency procurement., Must ensure inbound stock is set to Quarantine Pending status upon receipt.]], Eval[id=3, prompt=A standard order for 200 units of Chemical Z (SKU: CZ-300) is placed. DC-D has 150 units of Batch C1 (expiry: 2024-06-01, status: Available). The customer accepts split deliveries. The remaining 50 units are not in stock. The current stock level for CZ-300 is below the minimum threshold. Outline the allocation and replenishment actions., expectedOutput=The system must reserve the 150 available units from Batch C1. It must initiate a backorder for the remaining 50 units, respecting the customer's split delivery acceptance. It must trigger a replenishment request for at least 50 units (or more based on safety stock) from an approved supplier. The purchase requisition must be routed for financial approval based on the cost tier (e.g., if cost > £5k, requires Tier 1 approval)., files=[], expectations=[Must reserve 150 units from Batch C1., Must create a backorder for the remaining 50 units., Must trigger a replenishment request due to low stock levels., Must route the purchase requisition through the correct financial approval tier based on cost.]], Eval[id=4, prompt=A reservation for 10 units of Product W (SKU: PW-400) was made 50 minutes ago. The order is marked as 'Standard'. The system receives a warning that the reservation is about to expire. What actions should the system take, and what happens if the reservation expires?, expectedOutput=The system must send a 15-minute warning notification to the relevant team. Since the order is 'Standard', it must not automatically extend the reservation. If the reservation expires (at 60 minutes), the system must release the stock back to available inventory and recalculate availability for any pending orders. It must not silently substitute batches or hold the stock without explicit extension., files=[], expectations=[Must issue a warning at the 45-minute mark (15 minutes before expiry)., Must not auto-extend the reservation for a Standard order., Must release the stock back to available inventory upon expiry., Must recalculate availability for other orders after release.]]]]